user_prompt_template:
CHAPTER PLAN:
{current_chapter_json}

CHAPTER WALKTHROUGH NARRATIVE (read this carefully — your sheets must directly serve this content):
{chapter_narrative}

PROJECT CONTEXT:
Tutorial Request: {topic}
Document: {document_title}
Skill Level: {skill_level}
Stack: {stack}
Include Code: {include_code}
Output Style: {output_style}
Audience: {audience}
Tone: {tone}
Context: {context}

Design the checkpoint/reference/exercise sheets for {domain_name}. Every sheet must directly serve the walkthrough content in the narrative above and feel custom-built for this step of {topic}.

Before finalising each field label, ask: could this label appear unchanged in a sheet for a completely different tutorial? If yes, rewrite it until it cannot.

FOR EACH SHEET LISTED IN THE CHAPTER PLAN:
First, decide its format:
  → Is it a REFERENCE LIST of similar items (commands, env vars, endpoints)?  = "table"
  → Is it VERIFYING completion of discrete steps?                             = "checklist"
  → Is it COMPARING two states/options side by side?                          = "two-column"
  → Is it RECORDING, PLANNING, or an EXERCISE in narrative form?              = "form"

REPEAT-USE AND CROSS-REFERENCE FIELDS — required on every sheet:
  repeat_use (boolean): true if used on an ongoing or recurring basis (e.g. a smoke-test checklist); false for one-time setup.
  cross_references (array of strings): exact titles of sheets whose output feeds into this one or must be completed first.

SHEET DATA STRUCTURE BY FORMAT:

  layout: "table"
    Required: table_columns (array of 3–7 specific column header strings — not generic category names)
    Required: table_row_count (integer, 8–14)
    Required: sample_rows (array of 3 dicts mapping column headers to realistic pre-filled values from this stack)
    Required: common_errors (array of 2–3 step-specific mistakes)
    Omit: sections, fields

  layout: "checklist"
    Required: checklist_items (array of 10–20 complete verification statements — not single-verb tasks)
    Required: example_items (array of 3 fully completed example items showing what correctly-verified looks like)
    Required: common_errors (array of 2–3 step-specific mistakes)
    Omit: sections, fields

  layout: "two-column"
    Required: left_column_label, right_column_label
    Required: sections (2–4 sections, 3–5 fields each — same field structure as form)
    Required: common_errors (array of 2–3 step-specific mistakes)

  layout: "form"
    Required: sections (3–5 sections with distinct purposes)
    Each section: section_id, section_title, instructions (3–5 sentences naming prerequisites and defining completion), fields (4–8)
    Each field: field_id, label (hyper-specific to this step), type, placeholder (realistic specific value for this stack), required, validation_hint (correct-entry example), options (if select)
    Valid types: text, textarea, date, number, boolean, select, multi-select
    Required: common_errors (array of 2–3 step-specific mistakes)

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "chapter_number": {chapter_number},
  "domain_id": "domain ID from the chapter plan",
  "chapter_title": "Chapter title from the plan",
  "worksheets": [
    {{
      "id": "ws-{chapter_number:02d}-a",
      "title": "Exact title from chapter plan",
      "layout": "table | checklist | two-column | form",
      "purpose": "One sentence: the specific verification, reference, or practice output this sheet produces",
      "estimated_completion_time": "Realistic estimate, e.g. '10 minutes on first run, 3 minutes on re-checks'",
      "common_errors": ["Step-specific mistake 1", "Step-specific mistake 2"],

      "table_columns": ["Specific column header — not a generic category name"],
      "table_row_count": 10,
      "sample_rows": [{{"Column Header 1": "Realistic pre-filled value", "Column Header 2": "Realistic pre-filled value"}}],

      "checklist_items": ["Run/inspect [exactly what] from [where] — pass = [condition], fail = [first debugging move]"],
      "example_items": ["Example of a fully completed, correctly-verified checklist item"],

      "left_column_label": "Label for left column",
      "right_column_label": "Label for right column",

      "sections": [
        {{
          "section_id": "s-01",
          "section_title": "Specific section title naming its verification or output function",
          "instructions": "Before completing this section, [name what must be open/installed/done]. This section is complete when [verifiable condition — not just 'all fields filled'].",
          "fields": [
            {{
              "field_id": "f-001",
              "label": "Hyper-specific field label — could not apply to a different tutorial",
              "type": "text | textarea | date | number | boolean | select | multi-select",
              "placeholder": "Realistic specific example for this stack — not a generic placeholder",
              "required": true,
              "validation_hint": "Example of a correct, complete entry for this field in this tutorial",
              "options": []
            }}
          ]
        }}
      ],
      "decision_gates": [
        {{
          "gate_id": "g-01",
          "gate_title": "Gate name",
          "condition": "Specific verifiable condition from the narrative — command output, rendered behavior, or passing check",
          "pass_action": "What to do when the condition is met",
          "fail_action": "First debugging move when it is not",
          "blocks_completion": true
        }}
      ],
      "repeat_use": false,
      "cross_references": []
    }}
  ]
}}
